            ---
        ---
        # A field path is an ordinary expression: it only claims this statement
        # when the head is a real declared own field (an assignment into that
        # field). Any other head (return, a call argument, ...) falls through
        # to the general expression-value handling below -- a field path used
        # there resolves and reads through l2_eval_fields like any other value.
        # A path to a number field stored into an own field of another number type is a conversion, and a path to a
        # reference field is a reference: the general store below makes both (l2_convert_on_store; the reference read,
        # l2_path_record_read), as for any value (l2_path_store_general).
        if: l2_pstatus = 0 && (c.lm_compiler_own_visible(mi, (cast: (const: @: c.LmP0Text) (stmt\as\frame\head))) < 0 || lm_compiler_path_store_general_resolved(mi, (cast: (const: @: c.LmP0Text) (stmt\as\frame\head)), l2_ppath) != 0)
